Read `docs/build/README.md` first. Spec: `docs/specs/2026-10-25-powerbi-metrics-book.md`, sections The metrics book ("Metrics and variants", "Drafts: how the sync groups measures", items 1 to 4 and 6), Queries and results ("The query log": `measure_names`).

A pure module, no database and no I/O: `apps/api/src/dax/`. The drafter, the sync's rename detection and the query log consume it. It is conservative by design: a wrong match files two different calculations under one metric, which breaks the product's promise; a missed match only leaves work for an agent.

Produce exactly these exports from `src/dax/index.ts`:

```ts
export type DaxTokenKind = "keyword" | "function" | "table" | "column" | "identifier" | "string" | "number" | "operator" | "open" | "close" | "comma";
export type DaxToken = { kind: DaxTokenKind; text: string };   // text already normalised
export class DaxSyntaxError extends Error {}

export function tokenize(dax: string): DaxToken[];               // drops comments (//, --, /* */) and whitespace; throws DaxSyntaxError on an unterminated string, quoted table or bracket
export function normalize(dax: string): string;                  // tokens joined canonically: functions and keywords upper case, names case-folded, 'Sales' and Sales one way, numbers one way (1.0 and 1 the same)

export type MeasureMap = ReadonlyMap<string, string>;            // lower-cased measure name -> expression, one dataset
export function expandMeasures(name: string, measures: MeasureMap): { expanded: string } | { cycle: string[] };
export function fingerprint(expanded: string): string;           // SHA-256 hex of the normalised, expanded expression

export type Period = "current" | "previous_year" | "previous_quarter" | "previous_month" | "previous_week" | "previous_day" | "year_to_date" | "quarter_to_date" | "month_to_date" | "previous_year_to_date" | "rolling_12_months" | "other";
export type Comparison = "none" | "difference" | "growth_rate" | "ratio";
export type Shift = { period: Period; comparison: Comparison; comparison_period: Period | null };
export function recogniseVariant(name: string, measures: MeasureMap): { base: string; shift: Shift } | null;

export function readsSelection(expression: string): { reads: boolean; columns: string[] };
export function referencedMeasures(dax: string, measureNames: ReadonlySet<string>): string[];   // for the query log
```

Rules:

- `[X]` unqualified, or `'T'[X]`, is a measure reference when `X` is a measure of the dataset (case-insensitive); otherwise a column. `expandMeasures` replaces each measure reference with `(` its expanded expression `)`, recursively; a reference cycle returns the cycle's names in order.
- `recogniseVariant` looks at the measure's own top-level expression, before expansion, and matches only these shapes, with nothing else in them (an extra filter argument, a `FILTER`, a `KEEPFILTERS` makes it a different calculation and no match):
  - `CALCULATE([B], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(d))`, `CALCULATE([B], DATEADD(d, -1, YEAR))`, `CALCULATE([B], PARALLELPERIOD(d, -12, MONTH))`, `CALCULATE([B], PARALLELPERIOD(d, -1, YEAR))`: `previous_year`; `DATEADD(d, -1, QUARTER)`, `-1, MONTH`, `-1, DAY`: `previous_quarter`, `previous_month`, `previous_day`;
  - `TOTALYTD([B], d)`, `CALCULATE([B], DATESYTD(d))`: `year_to_date`; `TOTALQTD`/`DATESQTD`: `quarter_to_date`; `TOTALMTD`/`DATESMTD`: `month_to_date`;
  - `CALCULATE([B], DATESYTD(SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(d)))` and `CALCULATE([B_ytd], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(d))` where `B_ytd` is a `year_to_date` variant of `B`: `previous_year_to_date` of `B`;
  - `[B] - [B_p]`: comparison `difference`; `DIVIDE([B] - [B_p], [B_p])` and `DIVIDE([B], [B_p]) - 1`: `growth_rate`; `DIVIDE([B], [B_p])`: `ratio`; each where `[B_p]` is itself recognised as a period variant of `[B]`, and `comparison_period` is that period.
  `d` is any column reference. The base `B` is reported by its original measure name.
- `readsSelection` is true when the expression calls `SELECTEDVALUE`, `HASONEVALUE`, `ISFILTERED`, `ISCROSSFILTERED` or `ISINSCOPE`, and lists the columns those calls name.
- Never `eval`, never a regular expression over the whole expression for matching shapes: match on tokens.

Tests: table-driven (`src/dax/*.test.ts`), one row per pattern and at least one near miss per pattern that must not match (an extra filter, `DATEADD(d, -2, YEAR)` gives `null`, a comparison against a measure that is not a period variant, a different base on each side). Normalisation rows: case, quoting, whitespace, comments and number forms give one text; a changed column or function does not. Expansion: nested references, a cycle of three.

