Spec: `docs/specs/2026-10-27-phase-2-catalog-ui.md`. Read its "Settled by inspection" section first: those decisions were made by Martin looking at built screens and are not to be re-derived or changed. Read `apps/web/AGENTS.md`, `docs/standards/typescript.md`, `docs/decisions/look.md` and `packages/tokens/tokens.css` (every colour, size, radius and space is a token). Match the SPA's existing code: `src/shell/` (Shell, states, copy-button, time), `src/admin/layout/ui.tsx` (Button, PageFrame, SectionBox), `src/review/`.

Spec sections: Settled by inspection 2, 3, 4, 5, 6; Decisions (Keyboard); Built to be shared with Metrics Book (the `DiagramModel` types, copied below); Dependencies.

A self-contained component in `apps/web/src/catalog/diagram/` that imports nothing from `src/api` (Metrics Book will share it). React Flow (`@xyflow/react`) with a dagre layout (`@dagrejs/dagre`).

1. Add `@xyflow/react` `12.10.2` and `@dagrejs/dagre` `1.1.5` to `apps/web/package.json` dependencies, exact versions, and update `pnpm-lock.yaml` with `pnpm install`. Import `@xyflow/react/dist/style.css` in `apps/web/src/styles.css`, then override with tokens: `.react-flow { --xy-background-pattern-dots-color-default: var(--line-strong); }`, controls on `--surface` with `--line` borders, `--ink-2` icons, `--shadow-sheet`, radius `--radius`; hide `.react-flow__attribution`; `.react-flow__edge, .react-flow__node { cursor: pointer }`; `.react-flow__edge-path { transition: stroke 120ms ease-out, opacity 120ms ease-out }`.
2. `model.ts`, exactly:
```ts
export type DiagramTable = {
  name: string;
  description: string | null;
  columns: { name: string; type: string | null; hidden: boolean; pii?: boolean }[];
  measures: { name: string; folder: string | null }[];
};
export type DiagramRelationship = {
  from_table: string; from_column: string; to_table: string; to_column: string;
  cardinality: string | null; // "Many:One", as Power BI names it
  filters: "one_way" | "both_ways";
  is_active: boolean;
};
export type DiagramModel = {
  tables: DiagramTable[];
  relationships: DiagramRelationship[];
  /** Set when relationships are unknown: the sentence to show, no lines drawn. */
  unknown: string | null;
};
export type Density = "keys" | "all";
export type DiagramSelection = { kind: "table"; name: string } | { kind: "relationship"; index: number } | null;
```
3. `layout.ts`, pure functions: node width 232px, header 40, row 24, foot 26 (always present: "N more columns, M measures", or "M measures, no columns", or nothing when there is neither); `rowsFor(table, keys, density)` (keys only: the columns at either end of a relationship, in the table's column order; all: every column, the key ones marked); `layout(model, density)` with dagre `rankdir: "LR", nodesep: 28, ranksep: 120, marginx: 24, marginy: 24`, nodes added most-joined first, an edge per relationship from `from_table` to `to_table`; `grid(model, density)` for the unknown state (3 per row, 40px apart, each row as tall as its tallest table plus 24px); `ends(cardinality)` returning `["many" | "one", "many" | "one"]` (null reads as one to one); `viewport(bounds, pane, arrival?)`: zoom is the smallest of 1, the pane width less 64px over the bounds width, and the larger of 0.6 and the pane height less 64px over the bounds height; centred across; when the scaled height plus 64px exceeds the pane it starts 32px from the top, otherwise it is centred; with an arrival table, that table's middle is in the pane's middle.
4. `diagram.tsx`: `export function Diagram(props: { model: DiagramModel; density: Density; selection: DiagramSelection; onSelect(next: DiagramSelection): void })` and `export function Legend()`.
   - A table node: name in `text-ui font-semibold`; rows of `text-meta` with a lucide `KeyRound` (11px, stroke 1.75) for keys, `EyeOff` when Power BI hides the column, the type in `font-mono text-label text-ink-3`; the foot in `text-meta text-ink-3` above a `--line` border. Border `--line-strong`; selected: `--accent` border and a 2px accent outline; neighbour: `--accent` border; dimmed: opacity 0.45. Each row has a target handle on the left and a source handle on the right, zero-sized and invisible, ids `<column>:in` and `<column>:out`. Pass `width` and `height` on every node (the MiniMap reads them; React Flow did not report measured sizes through `onNodesChange` in the prototype).
   - A line: React Flow's default bezier edge from `<from_column>:out` to `<to_column>:in`. Markers in one hidden `<svg><defs>`, two tones (`plain` in `--ink-3`, `hot` in `--accent`), `viewBox="0 0 14 14" refX="13" refY="7" markerWidth="14" markerHeight="14" orient="auto-start-reverse" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse"`: many is `M1 7 L13 1 M1 7 L13 7 M1 7 L13 13`, one is `M6 1 L6 13`, stroke 1.25, no fill. `markerStart` from the from end, `markerEnd` from the to end. Stroke `--ink-3` 1.1px at rest, `--accent` 1.75px when hot; dashed `4 4` when inactive; label "inactive" or "both ways" in `--font-mono` 11px `--ink-3` on `--bg`; opacity 0.25 when another selection dims it.
   - Hot: the selected relationship, the selected table's relationships, the hovered line, the hovered table's lines. Hover dims nothing.
   - Click a table: `{ kind: "table" }`; click a line: `{ kind: "relationship", index }`; click the pane: `null`.
   - Dragging keeps positions (`onNodesChange` with `applyNodeChanges`) until `model` or `density` changes.
   - `panOnScroll`, `zoomOnScroll={false}`, `zoomOnPinch`, `minZoom 0.2`, `maxZoom 1.6`, `nodesConnectable={false}`, `nodesFocusable`. Dots background, gap 18. `Controls` bottom right without the interactive toggle. `MiniMap` bottom left only when the layout is taller than the pane, 140 by 110, `nodeColor` `var(--ink-3)`, `maskColor` `var(--select)`, `bgColor` `var(--surface)`, `pannable zoomable`.
   - The viewport from `viewport()` when the layout changes and when the selection goes from none to some or back (a panel opens beside it), 60ms after, so the pane has its new width. A table given as the selection when the layout first appears is the arrival table.
   - Keyboard: Enter on a focused table selects it; Escape clears the selection.
   - The unknown state (`model.unknown` set): `grid()`, no edges. The band with the sentence is the page's, not the component's.
   - `Legend`: the many to one line, the dashed inactive line, the key icon, the hidden icon, each with its word, `text-meta text-ink-3`.

Tests (vitest, `layout.test.ts`): rows per density (keys only, all, the foot's words); the same model laid out twice gives the same positions; `ends` for `Many:One`, `One:One`, null; `viewport` for a model that fits (centred), a tall one (top aligned, zoom at least 0.6, never above 1) and with an arrival table (its middle at the pane's middle); `grid` places 5 tables in 2 rows. A render test (`diagram.test.tsx`, testing-library as the SPA's other component tests do, or a plain `createRoot` in jsdom if none do): a model with an inactive relationship renders a dashed path and the label "inactive".

